course: dictionary
lesson: 1151
title: Brighten: light, mood and colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brighten is a verb, so it is a doing word. You will see it in four forms: brighten, brightens, brightened and brightening. It can mean becoming lighter, as in «The sky brightened after the rain».
explain: Brighten can also mean feeling happier, as in «Her face brightened», or making a place more colourful and pleasant, as in «Flowers brighten up the classroom». Look at the words around brighten to find out which meaning fits. Is something getting lighter, is a person getting happier, or is a place being made nicer?
explain: Brighten up and brighten someone's day are common phrases. When you meet a phrase you do not know, swap in a simple word such as lighter, happier or nicer, then read the sentence again to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Brighten is a verb, so it describes an action.
fact: «Brighten» can mean getting lighter, feeling happier, or making a place more colourful and pleasant.
fact: In weather reports, «it will brighten later» means the clouds will clear and the sun may come out.
fact: Brighten up and brighten someone's day are useful phrases to learn.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simple word, such as lighter or happier, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The sky brightened after the rain.» What does brightened mean here? | Became colder | Became louder | *Became lighter | Became wetter
exercise: «Her face brightened.» What does this show about her? | She was angry with her friend | *She suddenly felt happier and more hopeful | She felt tired and wanted to sleep
exercise: «Flowers brighten up the classroom.» Find and copy the word that means make more colourful and pleasant. | the | flowers | *brighten | classroom
test: In a weather report, «it will brighten later» means what? | The wind will stop completely | Rain will get heavier | It will snow all afternoon | *The clouds will clear and the sun may come out
test: A painter wants to brighten a dark picture. What should she do? | Cut the picture into small pieces | Cover it with a dark grey wash | Use only black paint | *Add lighter colours
exam: Which phrase means to make someone feel happier? | *brighten someone's day | drop someone's bag | count someone's steps
